# Stage D.1 — Docker build context exclusions.
# Keeps the build context small (faster builds, smaller cache) and prevents
# secrets / dev artifacts from leaking into the image.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Dependencies (will be installed fresh inside the builder stage)
node_modules

# Next.js build output (will be produced fresh inside the builder stage)
.next
.next-prod
.golden-scratch
.leadgen-data-e2e
readiness-proof

# Local data — NEVER bake into an image
.leadgen-data
.env*

# Tests + docs (not needed at runtime; keeps image small + reduces attack surface)
docs
# N-BUILD-2 (2026-08-20): exclude ALL of scripts/ and re-admit only the
# files the RUNTIME actually runs. The previous list named five script patterns
# and missed the rest, which broke the image build twice in a row for the same
# reason: `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts`, so `next build` type-checks every
# .ts left in the context, and a dev script that imports a helper from an
# EXCLUDED directory becomes "Cannot find module" — a failure that cannot
# reproduce locally, where the helper is present (`tsc --noEmit` is exit 0).
# First it was playwright.config.ts → ./e2e/helpers/data-dir; then
# scripts/probes/fresh-workspace-ai-probe.ts → ../golden/_helpers/provider.
# A deny-all + allow-list cannot drift that way: a new probe, smoke or golden
# is excluded by default, and anything the runtime needs must be named here on
# purpose. The two entrypoints below import only from `@/…` (src), which the
# image already carries — verified by grep, not assumed.
scripts
!scripts/worker-entrypoint.ts
!scripts/scheduler-entrypoint.ts
# 2026-09-09 (session 55): and the entrypoint the image's CMD actually runs.
# It was added to the Dockerfile without being re-admitted here, and the deny-
# all rule above swallowed it: the build died at
#   COPY scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh: "/scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh": not found
# so the change that makes migrations run before the server starts could not
# reach production at all. Nothing local reproduces it — the file is right
# there on disk; only the Docker build context is missing it.
!scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh
# 2026-09-27: the builder generates the demo site's sample company with these
# two (only src/ imports; no helpers from other scripts). Same trap as above:
# without them the build died "Cannot find module '/app/scripts/seed-demo.ts'".
!scripts/seed-demo.ts
!scripts/seed-demo-knowledge.ts
tests
playwright-report
test-results
e2e
# N-BUILD-2 (2026-08-20): playwright.config.ts must be excluded TOO, not just
# the e2e/ directory it imports from. tsconfig.json includes `**/*.ts`, so
# `next build` inside the image type-checked this root-level config file, and
# its first two lines import ./e2e/helpers/data-dir + ./e2e/helpers/e2e-target
# — which the line above had just removed from the context. The image build
# failed with "Cannot find module './e2e/helpers/data-dir'" while `tsc
# --noEmit` was exit 0 locally, because locally the files are there. It is a
# test harness config; nothing at runtime reads it.
# All local journey configurations import test helpers excluded above.
playwright*.config.ts

# Misc
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
Caddyfile
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CODEX_WORKING_RULES.md
Kimi_WORKING_RULES.md
AUTOMATION_*.md
NEXT_ACTIONS.md
.zcode
.agents
.claude
.playwright-mcp
.measure
.mutation-sweep
audit-mobile-out
Work Flow Images
fixtures
